# Spec section 5.6 stages everything (`git add -A`) so untracked files the
# agent created land in the submission diff. That is deliberate, and it also
# sweeps in anything the test run compiles: the first live smoke produced a
# diff whose first hunk was a binary __pycache__/calc.cpython-312.pyc.
#
# Every task repo in the dataset needs this, or diff size and file counts
# measure the interpreter rather than the agent.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
